Basic React App instructions:

- to create a new app: npm create vite@latest
  - enter the project name
  - specify "react" when prompted
  - specify "JavaScript" when prompted
- cd into the project directory
- to install dependencies: npm install
- to open the project in VS Code: code .
- once in VS Code, open a terminal window
- in the terminal window, to start the server in a browser tab run: npm run dev
- changes to the code will automatically be reflected in the browser tab
- debugging can be done using the browser's developer tools (F12)
- to stop the server, in the terminal window press: Ctrl + C

to deploy on github pages

- within VS Code, modify your vite.config.js (or vite.config.ts) file to include the base option. This is crucial for ensuring all assets are correctly referenced when served from a subfolder on GitHub Pages. Replace YOUR_REPOSITORY_NAME with the actual name of your GitHub repository.
- Install the gh-pages package:

      npm install gh-pages --save-dev

-Add the following script to package.json

    "scripts": {
      "dev": "vite",
      "build": "vite build",
      "predeploy": "npm run build",
      "deploy": "gh-pages -d dist"
    },

- Run deploy

      npm run deploy

- On github (on the web), make the repository public (at the bottom of Settings -> General)
- On settings->pages
- select 'deploy from branch' and select gh-pages as the branch and select save


To run from another device on the home network.

  npm run dev -- --host

The local URL will be listed as the second network item ('http://192.168.0.135:5173/swoop/', for example)